From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenBook <noreply@anybook.invalid>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] OPENBOOK: new app icons go on the first desktop page

AddWorkspaceItemsTask always skipped the first screen, which phones keep
for the search bar. OpenBook's desktop has no search bar on it, and the
launcher shows the first page by default, so every app installed from a
store put its icon on the second page, where the person did not see it:
their icons seemed to disappear whenever the launcher went back to its
first page (ANAL-220, on the G14).

Search for space from the first page.

Change-Id: I51cf6bd1abc457278ce1dad8850d982f6da7da31
---
 .../android/launcher3/model/tasks/AddWorkspaceItemsTask.java  | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/com/android/launcher3/model/tasks/AddWorkspaceItemsTask.java b/src/com/android/launcher3/model/tasks/AddWorkspaceItemsTask.java
index 1d511852d1..fe5b217272 100644
--- a/src/com/android/launcher3/model/tasks/AddWorkspaceItemsTask.java
+++ b/src/com/android/launcher3/model/tasks/AddWorkspaceItemsTask.java
@@ -78,7 +78,9 @@ public class AddWorkspaceItemsTask implements ModelUpdateTask {
         }
 
         final ArrayList<ItemInfo> addedItemsFinal = new ArrayList<>();
-        final IntSet excludedScreens = IntSet.wrap(FIRST_SCREEN_ID);
+        // OPENBOOK: the first page holds no search bar on OpenBook's desktop, and it is the page the launcher shows by
+        // default. Skipping it put every installed app's icon on the second page, where the person never saw it.
+        final IntSet excludedScreens = new IntSet();
         final Context context = taskController.getContext();
 
         synchronized (dataModel) {
-- 
